<section class="buyer-tools" aria-labelledby="roadmap-heading">
  <h2 id="roadmap-heading">A steady first pass</h2>
  <p class="roadmap-intro">Open each step for the short version of what it means and what to check next.</p>
  <div class="roadmap">
    <details>
      <summary><span class="step-number">1</span><span class="step-title">Name the questions you need answered</span><span class="step-control" aria-hidden="true"><span class="closed-copy">Open</span><span class="open-copy">Close</span><span class="step-mark">+</span></span></summary>
      <p>Separate what matters to your household from the facts that must be verified for a particular address.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary><span class="step-number">2</span><span class="step-title">Ask a licensed lender for current terms</span><span class="step-control" aria-hidden="true"><span class="closed-copy">Open</span><span class="open-copy">Close</span><span class="step-mark">+</span></span></summary>
      <p>Use a current lender review for financing terms and eligibility questions rather than a general estimate.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary><span class="step-number">3</span><span class="step-title">Understand representation before touring</span><span class="step-control" aria-hidden="true"><span class="closed-copy">Open</span><span class="open-copy">Close</span><span class="step-mark">+</span></span></summary>
      <p>A Texas license holder working with a prospective residential buyer generally must enter a written agreement before showing residential property. Review current TREC guidance before a property visit.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary><span class="step-number">4</span><span class="step-title">Verify each address on its own record</span><span class="step-control" aria-hidden="true"><span class="closed-copy">Open</span><span class="open-copy">Close</span><span class="step-mark">+</span></span></summary>
      <p>Compare taxes, insurance, flood information, restrictions, condition, and recurring costs for the property in front of you.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary><span class="step-number">5</span><span class="step-title">Read the offer as a set of terms</span><span class="step-control" aria-hidden="true"><span class="closed-copy">Open</span><span class="open-copy">Close</span><span class="step-mark">+</span></span></summary>
      <p>Inspection, appraisal, title work, lender review, and timing each answer a different question.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary><span class="step-number">6</span><span class="step-title">Keep the lending documents together</span><span class="step-control" aria-hidden="true"><span class="closed-copy">Open</span><span class="open-copy">Close</span><span class="step-mark">+</span></span></summary>
      <p>Read the Loan Estimate and closing documents with time to ask questions about the terms shown there.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary><span class="step-number">7</span><span class="step-title">Check assistance pages for current status</span><span class="step-control" aria-hidden="true"><span class="closed-copy">Open</span><span class="open-copy">Close</span><span class="step-mark">+</span></span></summary>
      <p>Official program pages are a place to confirm current status, not a promise about a benefit.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary><span class="step-number">8</span><span class="step-title">Confirm wire instructions independently</span><span class="step-control" aria-hidden="true"><span class="closed-copy">Open</span><span class="open-copy">Close</span><span class="step-mark">+</span></span></summary>
      <p>Use a contact method you already know when money or instructions change near closing.</p>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="buyer-tools glossary" aria-labelledby="glossary-heading">
  <h2 id="glossary-heading">A few terms worth keeping straight</h2>
  <dl>
    <div>
      <dt>Loan Estimate</dt>
      <dd>A lender document that helps you review the proposed loan terms and costs early in the process.</dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt>Closing Disclosure</dt>
      <dd>A closing document that helps you review the final terms and costs before completing the transaction.</dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt>Title work</dt>
      <dd>The review and documentation used to address ownership and title questions for a specific property.</dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt>Representation</dt>
      <dd>The role and agreement that define how a real estate professional may work with you in a transaction.</dd>
    </div>
  </dl>
</section>

